		(property "Note" "FAULT LED on the wired-OR open-drain fault line (eFuse FLT + TPS2553 FAULT): lit = over-current / over-temperature / OV clamp on a rail; the line is also read on GPIO47. Hubei KENTO KT-0603R, JLC basic (Economic-PCBA eligible; NationStar NCD0603R1 C84263 is Standard-PCBA-only per JLC's assembly review 2026-10-27). KENTO drawing: pad 1 = '+' (anode); C2286's LCSC symbol / footprint agree (pin 1 = A, layer-101 polarity dot on pad 1), so JLC's preview dot marks the ANODE on this part; fab_release.py maps it by the LCSC A / K pin names onto our A / K nets (DECISIONS #23)"
